  "instructions": [
    {
      "primary_message": "This recipe utilizes 2 large food storage containers.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Wash and dry the fresh produce.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "½ lemon\n1 stick celery\n½ small bunch green onion (scallion)\n½ small bunch fresh dill\n1 tomato\n½ head butter (Boston) lettuce"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Juice lemon into a medium bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Drain and rinse chickpeas. Add half of the chickpeas to the bowl with the lemon juice, along with mayo and spices. Using a fork or potato masher, mash until smooth. Add remaining whole chickpeas and stir to combine.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": "1 (254 g) can garbanzo beans (chickpeas)\n2 tbsp mayonnaise\n½ tsp curry powder\n¼ tsp turmeric, ground\n¼ tsp salt\n⅛ tsp black pepper"
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Small dice celery. Add to the bowl with the chickpea mixture.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Trim and cut green onions crosswise into thin pieces. Add to the bowl.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Shave dill leaves off the stems; discard stems and mince the leaves. Add to the bowl, stir to combine the chickpea salad, and set aside.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Slice tomato crosswise, then using a paper towel, pat tomato slices on both sides to remove excess liquid (this will help keep the wraps from getting soggy). Separate lettuce into leaves.\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    },
    {
      "primary_message": "Place flatbreads on a flat surface. Divide lettuce and tomato slices between them, then top with chickpea salad. Roll flatbread around the fillings, cut in half, then secure with parchment paper or plastic wrap if desired. Divide between the storage containers, along with apples, and refrigerate until ready to eat. Enjoy!\n\n\n\n",
      "secondary_message": null
    }
  ],
